  "goodToKnow": "Die Ortszeit is local time: um 10 Uhr Ortszeit. Germany uses MEZ (Mitteleuropäische Zeit, CET) and MESZ (summer time). Its official time is broadcast by the DCF77 radio signal from Mainflingen, based on atomic clocks at the PTB in Braunschweig, which sets radio-controlled clocks (Funkuhren) across Europe. Die Zeitzone is a time zone. Plural: die Ortszeiten."
